<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>6.1.6: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01580</md:content-id>
    <md:title>6.1.6: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>39a15d22-c944-4bf1-9086-737db5a436c2</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
<para>For questions 1 - 5, simplify each expression completely.</para>
<!--Do not edit this div tag.  It must surround the interaction block-->
<section><exercise id="_31411e4f-7669-41d2-bfa2-4c227dc837f1" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>\(14ab^2-8ab^2\)</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\(6ab^2\)</para><para>\(22ab^2\)</para><para>\(14ab^2\)</para><para>\(8ab^2\)</para></problem><solution><para>Try again. Revisit activity 6.1.2.</para><para>The correct answer is \(6ab^2\).

     </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="_1d91d1cd-1f5a-4d42-97b1-f8dca7a4f3ff" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>\((8k^2-3k+14)+(8k+17)\)</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Try again. Revisit activity 6.1.2.</para><para>The correct answer is \((8k^2+5k+31)\) .
     </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="_0f5a6c3b-f396-4007-bb7e-c4198ff89170" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>\((7b^2-2b-12)-(4b^2+9b-7)\)</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\(11b^2+7b-19\)</para><para>\(3b^2+7b-19\)</para><para>\(3b^2-11b-5\)</para><para>\(11b^2-11b-5\)</para></problem><solution><para>Try again. Revisit activity 6.1.2.
     </para><para>The correct answer is \(3b^2-11b-5\).
     </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="c6a07638-4de2-48b5-9d83-141c9a9539fc" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>\( (7mn^3-2m^2n-12mn)-(3mn^3-4mn)\)</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\(10mn^3-2m^2n-16mn\)</para><para>\(4mn^3-2m^2n-8mn\)</para><para>\(4mn^3-2m^2n-16mn\)</para><para>\(4mn^3-10m^2n\)</para></problem><solution><para>Try again. Revisit activity 6.1.2.</para><para>The correct answer is \(4mn^3-2m^2n-8mn\).
     </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="c8996f10-bb87-4d70-9349-cf59164cdd90" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>\( (r^3-r^2s)-2(rs^2+s^3)+(r^2s+2rs^2)\)</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\(r^3+2s^3\)</para><para>\(r^3-rs^2-2s^3\)</para><para>\(r^3-2s^3\)</para><para>\(r^3+rs^2-2s^3\)</para></problem><solution><para>Try again. Revisit activity 6.1.2.
     </para><para>The correct answer is \(r^3-2s^3\).
     </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="e60fdd8f-2742-4743-8f88-f7a439b07006" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Use the following polynomial functions to answer questions 6 – 10.</para><para>\(p(x) = 12x^2+3x-4\)</para>
        <para>\(d(x) = 3x^2-11x-6\)</para>
      <para>\( p(4)\)</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>-2</para><para>200</para><para>192</para><para>48</para></problem><solution><para>Try again. Revisit activity 6.1.3.</para><para>The correct answer is 200.</para></solution></exercise><exercise id="_8fcf5235-6283-48d4-9fc9-ad17a1884704" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>\(d(-3)\)</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>95</para><para>113</para><para>54</para><para>-12</para></problem><solution><para>Try again. Revisit activity 6.1.3.
     </para><para>The correct answer is 54.</para></solution></exercise><exercise id="e91603e4-fd35-4283-b26e-1992129584f9" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>\(p(x) + d(x)\)</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Try again. Revisit activity 6.1.4.
     </para><para>The correct answer is \(15x^2-8x-10\).
     </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="_3f34a974-1aba-4f60-adcf-6b92b4e3dd79" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>\(p(x) - d(x)\)</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Try again. Revisit activity 6.1.4.
     </para><para>The correct answer is \(9x^2+14x+2\).
     </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="_47d347ab-9731-419f-8748-37d9ece502a9" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>\( p(5) - d(-6)\)</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>143</para><para>311</para><para>168</para><para>479</para></problem><solution><para>Try again. Revisit activity 6.1.4.
     </para><para>The correct answer is 143.</para></solution></exercise></section></section>
